1
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,700
Reo...

2
00:00:15,690 --> 00:00:17,470
Yuka.

3
00:00:20,260 --> 00:00:22,590
You've grown taller.

4
00:00:25,170 --> 00:00:26,580
I guess so.

5
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:35,370
Reo, who is this?

6
00:00:36,570 --> 00:00:38,480
Yuka Oihara,

7
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:40,810
a senior from middle school.

8
00:00:40,810 --> 00:00:42,610
Nice to meet you.

9
00:00:42,610 --> 00:00:45,560
<i>[Yuka Oihara: Reo's senior from middle school. Taught him basketball, and winner of their middle school's beauty pageant]</i>

10
00:00:48,170 --> 00:00:50,480
This is Kasu—

11
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:53,270
Mai Toda.

12
00:00:53,270 --> 00:00:55,140
She's my girlfriend.

13
00:00:57,460 --> 00:00:59,640
Nice to meet you.

14
00:01:00,590 --> 00:01:05,150
I see. What a cute girlfriend.

15
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:08,600
Wow, what a coincidence!

16
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:11,850
No interrupting them, Ikumi.

17
00:01:11,850 --> 00:01:14,120
- Ken?
- Whoa,

18
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:16,130
Yuka?

19
00:01:16,150 --> 00:01:19,280
You haven't changed in these two years.

20
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:22,730
Y-You weren't meeting up with Reo, right?

21
00:01:22,730 --> 00:01:26,890
We just ran into each other. I was surprised.

22
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:32,250
You returned from Kagoshima?

23
00:01:32,250 --> 00:01:36,630
Yes, I have some business here. I'm going back in a week.

24
00:01:39,670 --> 00:01:43,280
I see. Why Kagoshima?

25
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:45,980
I'm attending university there.

26
00:01:46,910 --> 00:01:48,170
Interesting.

27
00:01:48,170 --> 00:01:50,160
Come on, let's go!

28
00:01:50,160 --> 00:01:51,610
Listen, Reo—

29
00:01:51,610 --> 00:01:54,950
Since we're busy, Ritsuki asked me to bring Mai as well.

30
00:01:54,950 --> 00:01:56,350
But it's my day off.

31
00:01:56,350 --> 00:01:58,350
This is cause you guys are slacking.

32
00:01:58,350 --> 00:02:00,450
See you, Yuka.

33
00:02:00,450 --> 00:02:02,330
Take care.

34
00:02:18,870 --> 00:02:22,830
<i>[Ai-Chan's Secret | Episode 8]</i>

35
00:02:23,290 --> 00:02:25,960
So she is your ex!

36
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:30,010
What were you doing with her, and your current girlfriend?

37
00:02:30,010 --> 00:02:32,440
We just coincidentally met.

38
00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:35,360
"Coincidentally"? Really?

39
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:39,200
He introduced you as his girlfriend, right?

40
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:41,460
You'll be fine.

41
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:45,180
Still, it feels like there's something between them.

42
00:02:46,140 --> 00:02:49,810
You can't help but be curious about an ex.

43
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:51,930
Yeah...

44
00:02:51,930 --> 00:02:55,160
Reo and Yuka were totally lovey-dovey.

45
00:02:55,160 --> 00:02:57,420
- Kenji.
- That's all in the past.

46
00:02:57,420 --> 00:03:00,230
She's only his ex.

47
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:07,150
<i>[Part-time Job: Egawatei]</i>

48
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:08,790
Hello?

49
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:12,710
Right now?

50
00:03:20,170 --> 00:03:22,790
Sorry we couldn't take it easy.

51
00:03:22,790 --> 00:03:24,410
It's fine.

52
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:28,100
I've already ended things with Yuka.

53
00:03:29,630 --> 00:03:31,090
Yeah.

54
00:03:47,540 --> 00:03:52,130
Sorry about this, Reo. The manager had business at the other branch.

55
00:03:52,130 --> 00:03:54,220
No worries.

56
00:03:54,220 --> 00:03:57,100
My plans got canceled anyway.

57
00:04:00,970 --> 00:04:02,640
Mai?

58
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:05,450
- Kasumi?
- Huh?

59
00:04:09,140 --> 00:04:12,380
I see you're worried about his ex-girlfriend.

60
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:13,910
Not at all.

61
00:04:13,910 --> 00:04:16,500
Isn't she Reo's first?

62
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:18,270
How can you tell?

63
00:04:18,270 --> 00:04:22,180
Watching them, it's obvious.

64
00:04:24,490 --> 00:04:28,670
If you waver and break, maybe there'll be space for me?

65
00:04:31,610 --> 00:04:34,140
Not a chance.

66
00:04:42,780 --> 00:04:45,520
Where's Hiroko?

67
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:48,680
She's busy in the office.

68
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:52,040
More importantly, the phone.

69
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:54,000
What about a phone?

70
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,820
You should check it.

71
00:04:56,820 --> 00:04:58,020
Why?

72
00:04:58,020 --> 00:05:02,050
His ex-girlfriend may be contacting him.

73
00:05:02,050 --> 00:05:05,680
Are you saying I should look at Reo's phone?

74
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:10,000
Obviously! What if he is contacting his ex?

75
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,810
He wouldn't.

76
00:05:12,810 --> 00:05:14,260
You're too naive.

77
00:05:14,260 --> 00:05:17,010
There are plenty of girls after him.

78
00:05:17,010 --> 00:05:21,770
Act so lax in this crisis, and you won't qualify as Reo's girlfriend!

79
00:05:23,220 --> 00:05:25,560
Not that I acknowledge you either.

80
00:05:30,530 --> 00:05:32,890
What? A "crisis"?

81
00:05:32,890 --> 00:05:36,280
She's overreacting.

82
00:05:36,280 --> 00:05:38,450
A crisis.

83
00:05:41,740 --> 00:05:43,860
Hiroko?

84
00:05:54,300 --> 00:05:57,750
Hiroko? What's wrong?

85
00:06:04,890 --> 00:06:08,080
The hell do you mean, you "cheated on her"?

86
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:12,000
- Ouch, what's wrong with you!
- Was your sincerity a lie?

87
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,960
I just went to a mixer as a favor, and my ex—

88
00:06:14,960 --> 00:06:17,700
Your ex-girlfriend?!

89
00:06:17,700 --> 00:06:20,380
Why go, when you have a girlfriend!

90
00:06:20,380 --> 00:06:24,920
It's a misunderstanding! Right now, I'm loyal to Hiroko.

91
00:06:26,630 --> 00:06:30,080
She was crying.

92
00:06:31,530 --> 00:06:33,370
She was?

93
00:06:36,270 --> 00:06:39,160
Hey, are you running?!

94
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:42,160
I won't forgive any cheating!

95
00:06:43,710 --> 00:06:47,850
An ex-girlfriend? Unforgivable.

96
00:06:47,850 --> 00:06:52,000
<i>[Ramen Egawatei]
[Open for business]</i>

97
00:07:06,900 --> 00:07:08,850
Hello?

98
00:07:08,850 --> 00:07:12,880
<i>I'm glad your phone number is the same.</i>

99
00:07:14,250 --> 00:07:15,910
Yuka?

100
00:07:20,990 --> 00:07:23,770
<i>[Reo]</i>

101
00:07:41,860 --> 00:07:43,850
What is it.

102
00:07:43,850 --> 00:07:45,460
<i>Well...</i>

103
00:07:48,170 --> 00:07:51,110
This afternoon was such a surprise.

104
00:07:51,110 --> 00:07:52,570
It was.

105
00:07:52,570 --> 00:07:56,250
<i>I've held onto this t-shirt </i>

106
00:07:56,250 --> 00:07:59,580
<i>I borrowed from you,</i>

107
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:01,730
<i>and I want to return it.</i>

108
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:05,970
Can we meet, just once?

109
00:08:06,630 --> 00:08:09,590
<i>You can throw it out.</i>

110
00:08:09,590 --> 00:08:11,860
- But —
<i>- Sorry.</i>

111
00:08:11,860 --> 00:08:13,800
I'm out of the house right now.

112
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:17,400
I… see.

113
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:19,650
In that case, I'll ask another time.

114
00:08:20,360 --> 00:08:24,740
My current girlfriend gets jealous easily,

115
00:08:25,320 --> 00:08:27,880
so I want to end it with this call.

116
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:34,620
I'm sorry.

117
00:08:34,620 --> 00:08:36,170
See you.

118
00:08:51,150 --> 00:08:54,910
<i>His ex-girlfriend may be contacting him.</i>

119
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:01,620
<i>[Kafuu High School]</i>

120
00:09:04,630 --> 00:09:09,040
<i>[Call History]
[Delete]</i>

121
00:09:13,330 --> 00:09:17,150
Listen, it's about yesterday...

122
00:09:18,010 --> 00:09:22,450
Sorry I didn't help with the whole Mai and Yuka situation.

123
00:09:22,450 --> 00:09:24,380
- You planned on helping?
- I did.

124
00:09:24,380 --> 00:09:29,220
I did, but… I got all excited.

125
00:09:29,880 --> 00:09:32,580
- Was Mai alright afterwards?
- Yeah.

126
00:09:32,580 --> 00:09:34,560
No need to worry about us.

127
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:38,800
What's with that confidence? I wasted my time worrying.

128
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:42,860
Besides, I won't meet with Yuka anymore.

129
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:47,430
- You've become a real man.
- And you sound high-and-mighty.

130
00:09:47,430 --> 00:09:51,870
Listen, you were in bad shape after Yuka's rejection.

131
00:09:51,870 --> 00:09:54,300
I couldn't watch you spiral.

132
00:09:54,300 --> 00:09:55,980
That's in the past.

133
00:09:55,980 --> 00:09:58,400
Deep down, I was worried.

134
00:09:58,400 --> 00:10:02,200
Thought you'd never fall in love again.

135
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:04,490
Love's amazing.

136
00:10:04,490 --> 00:10:06,940
Be grateful to Mai.

137
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:12,130
Hey, how're things going with Morikawa?

138
00:10:12,130 --> 00:10:14,220
Don't ask!

139
00:10:14,220 --> 00:10:15,800
Seriously, don't.

140
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:19,670
- And then?
- She has no love for me.

141
00:10:21,440 --> 00:10:26,550
Mr. Misato, one more lap, right?

142
00:10:26,550 --> 00:10:28,770
You're dawdling. Two more.

143
00:10:28,770 --> 00:10:32,590
- What?!
- Why is Koike so pissed?

144
00:10:32,590 --> 00:10:36,930
- I wonder—
- Why'd you just stop?

145
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:40,960
Look, it's Yuka.

146
00:10:44,490 --> 00:10:47,380
Is she the ex-girlfriend?

147
00:10:47,380 --> 00:10:48,740
Yeah.

148
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:51,840
She is pretty.

149
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:55,050
- Want to come watch us practice?
- No, I'm just...

150
00:10:55,050 --> 00:10:56,480
I thought you were going to "help out".

151
00:10:56,480 --> 00:10:59,140
Mai is not here, so it should be fine.

152
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:02,210
Let's go!

153
00:11:14,460 --> 00:11:16,770
You want to watch?

154
00:11:16,770 --> 00:11:18,750
Let's see...

155
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:22,200
Pardon me.

156
00:11:24,090 --> 00:11:25,610
Hello?

157
00:11:26,530 --> 00:11:28,970
The preschool, now?

158
00:11:28,970 --> 00:11:30,500
Yes, feel free to watch.

159
00:11:32,920 --> 00:11:35,200
What brings you here?

160
00:11:35,200 --> 00:11:36,560
I need to speak to Reo.

161
00:11:36,560 --> 00:11:38,380
- About what?
- Morikawa.

162
00:11:38,380 --> 00:11:40,640
I wanted to speak, face-to-face.

163
00:11:41,450 --> 00:11:43,160
Let's head on out.

164
00:11:49,130 --> 00:11:51,270
Mai, do something.

165
00:11:51,270 --> 00:11:52,300
Why me?

166
00:11:52,300 --> 00:11:55,880
She is Reo's senior. 1 on 1 her in basketball.

167
00:11:55,880 --> 00:11:58,300
- A 1 on 1?
- Exactly, now hurry!

168
00:11:58,300 --> 00:12:01,430
- No thanks, I don't wanna.
- What?!

169
00:12:01,430 --> 00:12:04,100
Yeah, quit while you can.

170
00:12:04,100 --> 00:12:07,630
She's not someone you can win against.

171
00:12:07,630 --> 00:12:11,010
Yuka was Reo's mentor.

172
00:12:11,010 --> 00:12:13,490
So there is no way you would win.

173
00:12:16,650 --> 00:12:19,780
- Nice job, Kenji!
- Nice job to what?

174
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:21,560
Excuse me.

175
00:12:22,760 --> 00:12:25,180
Go, go, Ai!

176
00:12:26,930 --> 00:12:30,980
My name is Aiko Kasumi.

177
00:12:30,980 --> 00:12:35,130
I'm somewhat of a… rival to Reo.

178
00:12:35,130 --> 00:12:36,860
His rival?

179
00:12:38,560 --> 00:12:42,920
Would you like have a 1 on 1 against me?

180
00:12:44,240 --> 00:12:45,890
What?

181
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:55,700
You'll play offense.

182
00:12:55,700 --> 00:12:58,220
That's my forte.

183
00:13:01,940 --> 00:13:05,630
Beat her to a pulp!

184
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:21,310
- She's really good.
- Is she?

185
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:38,280
How do you feel, seeing your ex and current girlfriend duel?

186
00:13:38,280 --> 00:13:40,070
Shut it.

187
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:50,760
You won't watch?

188
00:13:50,760 --> 00:13:52,860
Aiko is going to win.

189
00:14:04,270 --> 00:14:07,740
A two year break makes a difference.

190
00:14:07,740 --> 00:14:12,040
Not at all. I became desperate halfway through.

191
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:14,140
Really?

192
00:14:14,140 --> 00:14:18,580
You're good at the straightforward play style.

193
00:14:18,580 --> 00:14:20,670
Aiko, was it?

194
00:14:20,670 --> 00:14:23,520
Thank you, I had fun.

195
00:14:25,070 --> 00:14:26,870
Same here.

196
00:14:30,740 --> 00:14:34,210
I'm going to wash my hands. Are the sinks that way?

197
00:14:59,640 --> 00:15:01,140
Here you go.

198
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:04,690
May I? Thank you.

199
00:15:05,880 --> 00:15:08,360
What an innocent smile.

200
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:14,210
You have guts, coming to see your ex-boyfriend.

201
00:15:15,780 --> 00:15:18,160
Don't just lash out at her.

202
00:15:18,160 --> 00:15:20,280
Reo...

203
00:15:20,280 --> 00:15:24,450
This person is unexpectedly fragile.

204
00:15:30,410 --> 00:15:33,590
That's the wrong person to protect.

205
00:15:36,370 --> 00:15:40,040
Next time you mess up, I won't forgive you.

206
00:15:49,160 --> 00:15:50,790
Where is Reo?

207
00:15:50,790 --> 00:15:54,280
The bathroom?

208
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:57,660
Let's play a 1 on 1 ourselves.

209
00:15:57,660 --> 00:15:59,520
No, thanks.

210
00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:01,510
Why not?

211
00:16:01,510 --> 00:16:04,080
I wonder where he went.

212
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:20,080
You didn't come to return the t-shirt, did you?

213
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:23,100
I'm sorry, that was a lie.

214
00:16:25,710 --> 00:16:28,890
I really wanted to speak with you,

215
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,570
and meet once more.

216
00:16:37,420 --> 00:16:39,200
You're still...

217
00:16:40,610 --> 00:16:42,670
here.

218
00:16:43,850 --> 00:16:46,260
Reo, you linger in my heart.

219
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:51,890
Even when I transferred schools, and left for university.

220
00:16:53,190 --> 00:16:56,080
I often wonder what would've happened

221
00:16:57,130 --> 00:16:59,110
if we didn't break up.

222
00:17:00,990 --> 00:17:05,370
- That's why I came, and decided if I saw you—
- That's...

223
00:17:06,030 --> 00:17:08,200
already a thing of the past.

224
00:17:10,450 --> 00:17:11,950
I...

225
00:17:12,730 --> 00:17:15,810
seriously love my current girlfriend.

226
00:17:17,290 --> 00:17:19,270
That's why

227
00:17:19,270 --> 00:17:21,170
we won't meet anymore.

228
00:17:28,670 --> 00:17:30,710
Wait, Reo!

229
00:17:33,850 --> 00:17:36,110
I really...

230
00:17:36,110 --> 00:17:38,150
regret

231
00:17:39,660 --> 00:17:40,930
breaking up with you.

232
00:17:40,930 --> 00:17:43,350
You're the one who let go,

233
00:17:44,360 --> 00:17:46,020
Yuka.

234
00:17:50,330 --> 00:17:53,260
- I know, that's why—
- Sorry.

235
00:18:13,550 --> 00:18:16,280
♫ <i>What awaits in this battle of love?</i> ♫

236
00:18:16,280 --> 00:18:19,220
♫ <i>It seems it won't end in a draw</i> ♫

237
00:18:19,220 --> 00:18:22,280
♫ <i>You hated loosing,</i> ♫

238
00:18:22,280 --> 00:18:26,330
♫ <i>So I won't let you go easy on me</i> ♫

239
00:18:32,220 --> 00:18:34,720
You saw an unsightly part of me.

240
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:42,600
Thank you. You're kind.

241
00:18:42,600 --> 00:18:46,610
♫ <i>The secret that belongs to only us. 1on1</i> ♫

242
00:18:46,610 --> 00:18:49,820
"Be kind to girls",

243
00:18:49,820 --> 00:18:52,300
that's our family motto.

244
00:18:53,740 --> 00:18:55,680
How manly.

245
00:18:56,740 --> 00:18:58,980
I get told that often.

246
00:18:58,980 --> 00:19:05,160
♫ <i>Rather than touching, we can melt
into one another's embrace</i> ♫

247
00:19:05,160 --> 00:19:09,210
♫ <i>I'll let you get near just to return you like a wave</i> ♫

248
00:19:09,210 --> 00:19:11,130
You still...

249
00:19:13,350 --> 00:19:16,390
love Reo, don't you?

250
00:19:19,020 --> 00:19:21,160
Pathetic, aren't I?

251
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:27,610
I'm the only one

252
00:19:27,610 --> 00:19:29,920
stuck in the past.

253
00:19:31,440 --> 00:19:33,740
I can't move on.

254
00:19:36,030 --> 00:19:38,270
I feel like a fool.

255
00:19:38,270 --> 00:19:40,770
♫ <i>The bargaining is also clumsy</i> ♫

256
00:19:40,770 --> 00:19:44,450
♫ <i>I can’t beat you all the time</i> ♫

257
00:19:46,650 --> 00:19:50,760
Falling in love with someone...

258
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:53,210
feels amazing.

259
00:19:56,190 --> 00:19:59,300
Even ordinary sunset bring happiness

260
00:19:59,300 --> 00:20:02,320
when watching them with your crush.

261
00:20:03,110 --> 00:20:07,310
♫ <i>Deeper</i> ♫

262
00:20:09,540 --> 00:20:12,560
Worries easily build up

263
00:20:12,560 --> 00:20:15,620
when they don't contact you.

264
00:20:15,620 --> 00:20:18,790
Jealousy is nonstop,

265
00:20:18,790 --> 00:20:21,760
everything's confusing,

266
00:20:21,760 --> 00:20:24,950
and you can't be honest.

267
00:20:27,440 --> 00:20:30,230
It's all pretty pathetic.

268
00:20:32,480 --> 00:20:34,250
Seriously...

269
00:20:35,530 --> 00:20:37,960
how foolish.

270
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:41,760
♫ <i>Only I know this</i> ♫

271
00:20:41,760 --> 00:20:43,670
Even so...

272
00:20:43,670 --> 00:20:45,760
♫ <i>Rather than touching, we can melt
into one another's embrace</i> ♫

273
00:20:45,760 --> 00:20:48,890
the feeling of falling in love...

274
00:20:49,910 --> 00:20:52,580
♫ <i>I'll let you get near just to return you like a wave</i> ♫

275
00:20:52,580 --> 00:20:54,980
is something irreplaceable.

276
00:20:55,770 --> 00:21:00,670
♫ <i>I'll steal you away before anyone gets the chance</i> ♫

277
00:21:00,670 --> 00:21:03,070
♫ <i>Lips to exchange</i> ♫

278
00:21:03,070 --> 00:21:07,480
So, you have someone you love, too.

279
00:21:15,810 --> 00:21:17,480
Yeah,

280
00:21:18,450 --> 00:21:20,510
there is someone I like.

281
00:21:27,120 --> 00:21:28,990
I...

282
00:21:31,080 --> 00:21:33,620
love Reo Amano.

283
00:21:41,050 --> 00:21:43,570
<i>[Next time]
- Give up.
- It's not that easy.</i>

284
00:21:43,570 --> 00:21:45,280
<i>She's unexpectedly stubborn.</i>

285
00:21:45,280 --> 00:21:47,750
<i>- I'll cut it clean.
- A battle against his ex?</i>

286
00:21:47,750 --> 00:21:48,960
<i>It's fine if you look uncool.</i>

287
00:21:48,960 --> 00:21:51,290
<i>Yuka, you'll never disappear from within me.</i>

288
00:21:51,290 --> 00:21:53,430
<i>So I thought you'd pick Yuka over me.</i>

289
00:21:53,430 --> 00:21:56,050
<i>I want to break up with Mai.</i>
